{
  "id": "fruit-into-baskets",
  "questionId": "fruit-into-baskets",
  "slug": "fruit-into-baskets",
  "title": "Fruit Into Baskets",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "variable-size window",
    "at-most-k-distinct"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "'at most two baskets, one type each' is really just 'a window with at most 2 distinct values.' does that reframing remind you of anything?",
    "grow the window to the right, adding each fruit type to a running count map",
    "if the window ever holds more than 2 distinct types, shrink from the left, decrementing counts and removing a type entirely once its count hits zero, until only 2 types remain",
    "track the max window length as you go - this is the same 'at most k distinct' sliding window shape used in several other problems"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "removing a fruit type from the count map too early or too late relative to when its count actually reaches zero",
    "shrinking the window by more than one step at a time, potentially skipping a valid shorter window",
    "confusing 'at most 2 distinct types' with 'exactly 2 distinct types', which changes edge cases like an all-one-type array"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a row of fruit trees, represented as a list where each\nnumber is the type of fruit at that position. You have exactly two\nbaskets, and each basket can only hold a single type of fruit, but any\namount of it.\n\n**Starting anywhere, pick fruit from consecutive trees until you'd need a third type, and return the maximum number of fruits you can collect this way.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= fruits.length <= 10^5",
      "0 <= fruits[i] < fruits.length"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "only one type of fruit in the whole row",
      "every tree is a different type",
      "a single tree"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
